# Architecture

## Directory responsibilities

| Path | Owns |
|------|------|
| `app/` | App Router routes, layouts, loading/error boundaries |
| `app/actions/` | Server Actions (`"use server"`) |
| `components/ui/<Name>/` | Reusable, domain-agnostic UI primitives |
| `components/custom/<Name>/` | App-specific composed components (pages, forms, shells) |
| `components/providers/` | Application-wide React context wrappers |
| `lib/` | Framework-agnostic shared utilities (no UI, no route dependencies) |
| `styles/tokens/` | Design tokens — consumed centrally by `app/globals.css` |

## Dependency boundaries

- `app/` may import from `components/` and `lib/`.
- `components/` may import from `lib/` and from Server Actions in `app/actions/` only. Must not import pages, layouts, or `lib/supabase/admin.ts`.
- `lib/` must not import from `components/` or `app/`.
- Import project modules via the `@/` alias (maps to repo root per `tsconfig.json`).

## React rendering boundary

- Use Server Components by default.
- Add `"use client"` only when browser APIs, event handlers, state, effects, or client-only hooks are required.
- Keep client boundaries as close as possible to the interactive element.

## UI component structure

Each component lives in `components/ui/<ComponentName>/` (primitives) or `components/custom/<ComponentName>/` (app-specific):

```
<ComponentName>.tsx        # implementation (Server Component by default)
<ComponentName>.types.ts   # exported types
index.ts                   # barrel re-export of component and types
```

## Design-token flow

```
styles/tokens/primitives/brand.css   (--p-*)
        ↓
styles/tokens/semantic.css           (--bg-*, --fg-*, component slots)
        ↓  mapped in @theme inline
app/globals.css                      (Tailwind utilities: bg-canvas, text-fg …)
        ↓
components — use Tailwind semantic utilities only
```

Components must never reference `--p-*` primitive tokens. Tokens are imported only through `app/globals.css`.
